From 4eb050f06090ddb6416ef59b7a6fb4da714208be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Begonia <begonia@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:26:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/18] power: supply: Add MediaTek MT6359 PMIC fuel gauge
 driver

The MT6359 PMIC has a coulomb counter and a current ADC (FGADC) that
measure the battery current in both directions over a sense resistor.
There was no mainline driver for it, so a board with this PMIC had no
usable battery power supply (the charger ADC only sees charge current).

Add a driver, instantiated as an MFD cell of the PMIC, that registers a
"battery" power supply. Current and charge flow come from the FGADC; the
starting point and the slow drift correction use the open circuit voltage
with the OCV table and internal resistance of the simple-battery node.
Register layout and LSB values follow the downstream mt6359_gauge.c.
